ype\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"9fa174cfb89c384357295a90ca65f917c76e72e5c89dc27a4ea861c74d2503fc","event_uuid":"6d7785de-e346-4489-8b31-d9eb774dbae3","position":{"commit_sha":"af6b823902042a71d974e2962810d02256ae54cd","position":"1795131020134477001-6d7785de-e346-4489-8b31-d9eb774dbae3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"87d82379c10cf8cec96cf67561c105eb2c4eb60d91f1b060eae7cffa223b17c8","event_uuid":"5c0b7d81-c8ae-4ad1-ac17-82039f5c0743","position":{"commit_sha":"a4e90c808e4c2d7ec37dee0538972b02372b6a2e","position":"1795131035878773001-5c0b7d81-c8ae-4ad1-ac17-82039f5c0743"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"env_integration","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause confirmed (AC1). The test's `_StubServer` had no drain gauge, so the boot-sweep thread `main()` starts (`start_startup_store_sweep`, `mcp_server.py:583`) was untracked, and `run_mcp`'s `wait_for_idle` had nothing to wait for. `main()` returned right after the stub `run`, and the `['ensures', 'run']` assertion raced the thread. Production always has a gauge (`wire_health`), so main() there waits for the sweep. Evidence: a fake sweep delayed 0.5 s fails the old test on macOS every time with `['run'] == ['ensures', 'run']`, the Windows signature.\n\nFix (commit 20015971a04, worktree a4-moth-boot-sweep-gauge, test-only): the stub carries an `InFlightGauge`, and the test is now `test_mcp_startup_sweep_completes_before_main_returns`. Its sweep blocks until `run` starts, and it asserts `['run', 'ensures']`, the async contract: main() does not return before the sweep finishes. RED without the gauge: `assert ['run'] == ['run', 'ensures']`, every time. GREEN with it. The goose cleanup test (bare `object()` server) now stubs the sweep, as test_mcp_idle_sync already does. 43 passed across test_fsck_ensures, goose, startup_sweep_background and idle_sync. Portable: threading.Event and the existing gauge only.","timestamp":1795115815394902347},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3463 merged as 0fec72331c467dce8759c69f8b8ae829ca184a53. make verify passed before the push (21,500 passed, 30 skipped; integration 226 passed, 2 skipped; exit 0).\nWindows: run 44621093373, `sweep (windows)` job 135902646205, at main 0fec72331c4, concluded `success` (20,269 passed, 872 skipped, 0 failed). The replacement test `test_fsck_ensures.py::test_mcp_startup_sweep_completes_before_main_returns` ran there (the job log carries its rebar-ci-timing warning, worker gw2) and is not among the failures, since there are none. Closing as env_integration.","timestamp":1795130335180611001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1795108864806385038,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"787c7a78-fb2f-4af5-a384-1db7d90d4e5e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d307-72a6-284a-46e7"},{"link_uuid":"5c0b7d81-c8ae-4ad1-ac17-82039f5c0743","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"b173-e50a-4b93-455f"}],"description":"## Observation\n\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_ensures.py::test_mcp_startup_sweeps_before_run` failed in `sweep (windows)` job 135688612206 (run 44560626779, main at 91322a91e9ed31b0523451b678cf2b3a40cdff8b): `AssertionError: run_ensures must precede build_server().run()`, with `order == ['run']`. It passed in the 3 previous Windows sweeps (jobs 135490319213, 135569438854, 135597358757). That makes it intermittent.\n\nSince 5029b61749d (\"Run MCP boot ensure sweep after listen\"), `mcp_server.main()` starts the boot sweep on a background thread (`start_startup_store_sweep`, `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:403`) and then calls `run_mcp`. The test stubs `build_server().run` and asserts the order `['ensures', 'run']`, which only holds if the thread wins the race. An earlier order-dependence bug on this test, solid-velour-lynx (de95-1594-1056-436e), is closed. Its assertion message, `got ['run']`, matches this failure.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed)\n\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:583` passes `getattr(server, _GAUGE_ATTR, None)` to `start_startup_store_sweep`. The sweep thread holds that gauge until it ends (`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:403-421`), and `run_mcp` waits for the gauge to reach 0 before returning (`src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py:197-209`, `wait_for_idle` at line 51). That wait is the only thing that makes `main()` return after the sweep. `build_server` always wires a gauge (`wire_health`, `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:572-585`), so production never runs without it.\n- The test's `_StubServer` (`tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_ensures.py:129-135`) has no gauge attribute. Its sweep thread is therefore untracked: `main()` returns as soon as the stub `run` records `'run'`, and the assertion reads `order` before the thread may have appended `'ensures'`.\n- The asserted order is also not the code's contract. Since 5029b61749d the sweep is deliberately allowed to finish after serving starts (`tests/unit/test_mcp_startup_sweep_background.py::test_main_reaches_run_mcp_while_the_boot_sweep_is_still_running`).\n- Experiment: delaying the faked `run_ensures` by 0.5 s makes the test fail deterministically on macOS with `assert ['run'] == ['ensures', 'run']`. Without the delay the thread usually wins, which is why it passes most runs.\n- Same class: `test_mcp_startup_never_aborts_on_sweep_error` (same stub) and `tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py:483` (`build_server` returns a bare `object()`) also leave an untracked boot-sweep thread that can outlive the test and its monkeypatches.\n\n## Approach\n\nProduction code is correct, so the fix is in the tests: give them the gauge `build_server` provides, and assert the async contract instead of a thread race.\n- `_StubServer.__init__` sets `_GAUGE_ATTR` to a real `InFlightGauge`, so `run_mcp`'s idle wait covers the sweep exactly as in production.\n- Replace `test_mcp_startup_sweeps_before_run` with `test_mcp_startup_sweep_completes_before_main_returns`. Its faked `run_ensures` blocks until the stub `run` has started (a `threading.Event`, bounded by a 30 s ceiling), which forces the run-first interleaving the old test raced on. It then asserts `order == ['run', 'ensures']` after `main()` returns: the sweep ran, and `main()` did not return before it finished.\n- In the goose test, stub `start_startup_store_sweep` the way `tests/unit/test_mcp_idle_sync.py:304` already does, because that test is about binding cleanup, not the sweep.\nNo production code, config key, env var or flag changes.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_ensures.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py`\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED: with the gauge-less stub, the new test fails deterministically (`main()` returns with `['run']`, because the sweep is blocked until after `run`). GREEN once the stub carries a gauge.\n- `test_mcp_startup_never_aborts_on_sweep_error` and `test_mcp_help_skips_sweep` stay green; the goose test stays green.\n- `make verify`.\n\n## Portability\n\nUses only `threading.Event` and the existing gauge, with no OS-specific API. The ordering no longer depends on thread scheduling, which differs most on Windows runners.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The ordering the test asserts is either guaranteed by the code under test or replaced by an assertion that matches the async contract (for example, the sweep has completed before shutdown). The root cause is recorded with evidence.\n- [x] `make verify` passes, and a `sweep (windows)` job on main after the fix does not list this test among its failures.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_ensures.py","reason":"give the stub server a drain gauge and assert the async boot-sweep contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py","reason":"stub the boot sweep so no untracked sweep thread outlives the test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","d307-72a6-284a-46e7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6c2eed1e-9757-48f1-b528-09cf15f231f9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["windows","flaky"],"ticket_id":"a5be-a825-30ea-4f09","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_mcp_startup_sweeps_before_run races the background boot sweep thread (Windows sweep)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a1f6133b-9973-4932-ae96-d7d2cff5b8f1","19f22b67-a0df-4c96-8168-f84a36c2a82c","b07d88cc-3e7d-4438-8990-ee559f39d9ca","5de15150-3294-41ca-9f50-db81c3b3c7b4","8fabc151-cbd1-40f2-a0d7-eaddb32908cb","8c590ca9-40f2-4293-8134-7974b9e90cc0","4c286aa1-8a7e-4d67-be35-911695ae19eb","787c7a78-fb2f-4af5-a384-1db7d90d4e5e","6e5faacd-4e10-48cb-a562-1b1850ba6bee","44c6c0bf-246f-4fb4-84c2-03ff12a14eda","c429ec2d-c53b-4588-be7b-d3a3cd29288c","6c2eed1e-9757-48f1-b528-09cf15f231f9","6d7785de-e346-4489-8b31-d9eb774dbae3","5c0b7d81-c8ae-4ad1-ac17-82039f5c0743"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795131035878773002,"uuid":"2595f456-0ae0-4c11-b9e3-80fb9f340e42"}
